  "question": {
    "text": "Which pair of oxides is acidic in nature?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CaO</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BaO</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CaO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An oxide that combines with water to give an acid is termed as an acidic oxide. The oxide that gives a base in water is known as a basic oxide. An amphoteric solution is a substance that can chemically react as either acid or base.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> both are oxides of non-metal and hence are acidic in nature.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>CaO</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>BaO</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Basic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Nature</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Acidic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Nature</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Neutral</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>oxide</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
